== Method chosen by the tester (no steps in the DB)
Link: x230 port1.0.1 (AT-SPTXa copper SFP) <-> AR4050S port1.0.2 (fixed copper, 10/100/1000, half and full). It is the only
x230 link whose partner runs 10 Mb/s and half duplex (T47208: the IE520 SFP ports refuse 10; eth3 is a host NIC, root to
change). The x230 sends the IEEE 802.3 MAC/PHY Configuration/Status TLV (`lldp tlv-select mac-phy-config`); the 4050 decodes
it in `show lldp neighbors detail`. For each user-defined combination: change the x230 (and, for forced modes, the 4050
first), wait for the x230 port to connect, then poll the 4050 until the TLV shows the expected fields.
Expected TLV fields per IEEE 802.3 Annex 79 (Auto-negotiation support/status, advertised capability, operational MAU type):
  autoneg (speed auto [<list>], duplex auto|half) -> "Supported, Enabled", advertised = exactly the restricted set,
     MAU = the negotiated speed/duplex;
  forced (speed <n> + duplex full|half on both ends) -> "Supported, Disabled", advertised [none], MAU = the forced pair.

