== Summary
All 9 combinations: the x230's MAC/PHY TLV, as decoded by the AR4050S, carried the right autoneg status, advertised set and
operational MAU type for the user-defined speed/duplex/autoneg; the link came up at the configured speed and duplex each time.
Observation (not graded as a fault): with `speed 1000` + `duplex full` (C8) the x230 reports autoneg "Supported, Disabled"
  and advertised [none] while the 4050 end reads a-full a-1000. 1000BASE-T always negotiates (clause 40), so the x230 PHY
  still auto-negotiated 1000/full only; the TLV reflects the configured (fixed) mode. Worth a note for the case owner.
Status-column note (C3): `speed auto 100` + `duplex half` reads "half   a-100" on the x230 (the duplex is configured, not
  negotiated), so the status regex expecting "a-half" timed out; the link and the TLV (100BaseTXHD, Enabled, 100BaseTX
  advertised) were correct.

Run: clean.
VERDICT: PASS -- for 9 user-defined speed/duplex/autoneg combinations (auto, auto-100, auto-100-half, auto-10, fixed 1000, forced 100/10 full/half) the x230's MAC/PHY TLV decoded at the AR4050S showed the matching autoneg state, advertised set and MAU type
